-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ABOUT ENTERPARAMETERS.TXT:
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
enterparameters.txt is the only input method you should need for basic applications

You SHOULD write Naca, naca or NACA on every line start. This won't be fixed
because eventually some other airfoil standards outside of NACA are to be added

The file will be parsed expecting comma seperated values (12,ABC,53...)

Position parameter is defined with respect to origin and YZ as the datum plane.
However, you can add a "+" sign before the position numerical value to specify
distance to last section. This is just a wrapper to take last position and add
the distance, specifying a new workplane.

Comments at the end of a line may cause unintended behaviour, please write
comment and content lines seperately

 